DATABASE
======================================================================
  New column Order.problemReportedAt (timestamptz, nullable): additive, no data changed.
  npm run db:update -- --dry-run: 1 operation, ALTER TABLE "public"."order" ADD COLUMN
  "problemReportedAt" timestamptz. Applied ("Applied 1 operation(s)"); second dry run: 0.
  Checked directly in Supabase (aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com): columns
  chatClosedAt and problemReportedAt both present. (db:update now reads .env, see the
  previous log: it went to Supabase this time, not to the local Postgres.)

